  "answer_text": "Under standard food safety guidelines (such as the FDA Food Code and ServSafe), the temperature at which food can be accepted during delivery depends entirely on the type of food. \n\nHere are the specific receiving temperatures required for food to be safely accepted:\n\n### 1. Cold TCS Foods (Time/Temperature Control for Safety)\n* **Acceptance Temperature:** **41\u00b0F (5\u00b0C) or lower**.\n* **Examples:** Fresh meat, poultry, fish, dairy (other than milk), cut melons, cut tomatoes, and leafy greens.\n\n### 2. Hot TCS Foods\n* **Acceptance Temperature:** **135\u00b0F (57\u00b0C) or higher**.\n* **Examples:** Prepared hot dishes, rotisserie chickens, or buffet items being delivered hot.\n\n### 3. Frozen Foods\n* **Acceptance Requirement:** Must be **frozen solid** upon delivery.\n* **When to Reject:** Reject the delivery if there are signs of thawing and refreezing, such as fluid/water stains on the packaging or large ice crystals on the product.\n\n### 4. Special Exceptions (Shellfish, Milk, and Eggs)\nSome items can be accepted at slightly higher temperatures, provided they meet specific cooling and storage criteria:\n\n* **Shell Eggs:** Must be received at an ambient/air temperature of **45\u00b0F (7\u00b0C) or lower**.\n* **Milk:** Must be received at **45\u00b0F (7\u00b0C) or lower**, and must be cooled to **41\u00b0F (5\u00b0C) or lower within 4 hours** of receipt.\n* **Shucked Shellfish:** Must be received at **45\u00b0F (7\u00b0C) or lower**, and must be cooled to **41\u00b0F (5\u00b0C) or lower within 4 hours**.\n* **Live Shellfish (Oysters, Mussels, Clams, Scallops):** Must be received at an air temperature of **45\u00b0F (7\u00b0C)** and an internal temperature no greater than **50\u00b0F (10\u00b0C)**. Once received, they must be cooled to **41\u00b0F (5\u00b0C) or lower within 4 hours**.\n\n---\n\n### How to Correctly Check Temperatures During Receiving:\n* **Meat, Poultry, and Fish:** Insert the clean, sanitized thermometer probe directly into the thickest part of the food (usually the center).\n* **Reduced-Oxygen Packaged (ROP/MAP/Sous Vide) Food:** Place the thermometer probe between two packages. **Do not puncture** the packaging.\n* **Other Packaged Foods (like milk cartons):** Open one package and insert the thermometer probe directly into the liquid. Do not let the probe touch the sides or bottom of the container.",
